Z||000001||theogre||10-15-2000||11:50 AM||||try installing a heat shield for the starter. That may help. You'll likely need to replace the starter or the solinoid.<P><BR>I didn't think you could adjust the fuel pressure regulator in the 220 & 300 family TBI without tearing it apart. The 700 TBI used 87+up is adjustable without any disassembly but the hole is plugged.<P>There's little reason to play with fuel pressure unless the motor has some sort of major midifications. If you are going to play with that go and get a fuel pressure guage for it.<P>You have to remove what is plugging the hole so you can get to the screw. Never bothered to mess with that. couldn't tell you how to best clear the access.<P><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-15-2000).]||||reg||1
